Chapter: E1000SwflagMng
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Kernel chapter E1000e
  cites Kernel chapter Pci

Section: Fixtures

  dev-id-of : PciScanResult -> Integer
  dev-id-of (scan) =
    when e1000-find scan
      is Just (d) -> (d.pci-device-id)
      is None -> 0

  bring-up : PciScanResult -> E1000Device
  bring-up (scan) =
    when e1000-find scan
      is Just (d) -> e1000-init d
      is None -> e1000-absent

Section: Judges

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

Section: Entry

 THE CASE A DRIVER THAT ASSUMES IT ALWAYS WINS CANNOT SURVIVE. Firmware holds
 MNG ownership, so the acquisition is refused however correct the protocol is,
 and 82583V 4.5.2 is explicit that MNG "is reset only by LAN_PWR_GOOD (or if
 the firmware clears it)" -- there is nothing this driver can do to take it.

 THIS IS THE ARM THAT MAKES `e1000-swflag` MEAN SOMETHING. That arm's acquire
 succeeds, and an acquire that cannot fail is not evidence that the protocol
 was followed: a function that unconditionally answered 1 would pass it. Here
 the same call must answer 0 and leave the bit clear, and `mng holds` shows the
 reason is the other agent's bit rather than a broken call.

 IT ALSO ASSERTS THE FUEL TERMINATES. `e1000-swflag-acquire` retries until it
 reads its own bit back, so a refusal that never ends is a hang rather than a
 red, and a row printed after it is the proof it returned.

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let scan = pci-scan-bus 0
    in let did = dev-id-of scan
    in let d = bring-up scan
    in let mmio = d.e-mmio
    in let ext = e1000-read mmio e1000-reg-extcnf-ctrl
    in let got = e1000-swflag-acquire mmio e1000-swflag-fuel
    in let held = e1000-swflag-held mmio
    in act
      print-line-uni ("part is pch        : " & yn (e1000-pch-part did))
      print-line-uni ("mng holds          : " & yn (bit-and ext e1000-extcnf-mng-own /= 0))
      print-line-uni ("acquire answers    : " & show got)
      print-line-uni ("flag held          : " & yn held)
    end
  end

